{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1252353-explain-me-rotes","id":1252353,"title":"Explain me Rotes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-07T14:31:40-07:00","id":1252353,"title":"Explain me Rotes","content":"If I remember correctly in Mage the Awakening 1ed Rotes where pre-built spell casted using Att + skill+ Arcanum.<br /> <br /> I was reading the 2nd edition of Awakening and I saw the things quite changed.<br /> <br /> 1) What's now the difference between Rotes and Improvised spells? Do they use both Gnosis + Arcanum?<br /> 2)Rituals can be done now with improvised spells?<br /> 3)How do Mudras works?<br /> 4) What are the &quot;suggested skill&quot; for rotes after each spell in the spell sections? (probably this will get an asnwer after you will answer the first or third question...but nevertheless...)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T15:12:01-07:00","id":1252366,"title":"","content":"1. All spells roll Gnosis + Arcanum. A spell cast as a praxis rolls exceptional successes more easily (on three rolled successes instead of five). A spell cast as a rote calculates Reach (but not dice pool) as if you had five dots in the Arcanum, and if cast as an extended ritual directly out of the grimoire, applies the rote quality (reroll failed dice). Neither praxes nor rotes cost Mana to cast spells outside your Ruling Arcana, unlike improvised casting.<br /> <br /> 2. Improvised spells can be performed in ritual casting time. As a matter of fact, you have to exert a reach to move an improvised spell <i>out</i> of ritual casting time; it is the baseline.<br /> <br /> 3. A mudra is an extremely potent yantra or magical focus which is part of the teaching of a rote spell. If you know a rote, you may perform its mudra as an action while building up to casting the rote. The mudra yields a dice bonus to your spellcasting equal to your rating in the rote's mudra Skill (plus a die if it's one of your Order's Rote Skills). This is technically distinct from simply having a dice pool of Gnosis + Arcanum + Skill because the number of yantras you can apply to one spell is limited, and because the sum of all your yantra bonuses on the spell is capped at +5.<br /> <br /> 4. They're common suggestions for possible mudra Skills for rotes of that Skill. Rotes are varied but not fluid. This is to say three masters may each encode a rote for the same spell, and if they focus and formulize it differently, those rotes can all have different mudra Skills: rotes are varied. A student studying from a grimoire, however, will cast the rote he learns using the mudra Skill encoded in that taught rote, regardless of whether another master's rote somewhere uses a mudra the student would grasp better: rotes are not fluid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 09-07-2018, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T15:15:37-07:00","id":1252369,"title":"","content":"1.a) Rotes doesn't cost a Mana to cast from common or inferior Arcana, have access to the Mudra Yantra (which adds your character's rating in a chosen Skill) if cast from memory, and grants Rote Action if cast from a Grimoire (or if you personally created the Rote).<br /> 1.b) The dice pool is the same for both, but Rotes grants access to a Mudra and/or Rote Action depending on how you cast it.<br /> 2.) Yes.<br /> 3.) Mudra is used as a Yantra. The dice bonus equals the mage's rating in the chosen Skill (to a maximum of 5) and adds one extra die if the Skill is one of the mage's Order Rote Skills.<br /> 4.) Every Rote is connected to a Skill (which is used for the Mudra). The three provided are examples for what Skill that spell might have as a Rote. They might instead use an unlisted Skill if that Skill would make sense for the Rote, but the three listed are the most common Skills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 09-07-2018, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T18:29:44-07:00","id":1252411,"title":"","content":"Rotes still have reduced Paradox, don't they?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T19:02:45-07:00","id":1252418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1252353-explain-me-rotes?p=1252411#post1252411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rotes still have reduced Paradox, don't they?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of, you\u2019re less likely to risk Paradox because of the Reach bump.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T21:16:44-07:00","id":1252433,"title":"","content":"Also, if you have a grimoire holding the Rote you can take a *lot* of extra time to gain the Rote quality for the spell, meaning that any dice that fail on the first roll, you re-roll. That's in addition to the skill bonus (if you've actually learned the rote as well as having it in the grimoire) and the extra Reach (which you get either way).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T10:48:21-07:00","id":1252548,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers, I am tempted to use Awakening rules with Ascensions spheres and setting, so I needed some clarifications. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T19:59:53-07:00","id":1252647,"title":"","content":"Rote spells also gain the Rote quality if you are the one who made it, not just if it's from a grimoire. Though, use of grimoires is going to be the most common way to get that benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T13:24:33-07:00","id":1253366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1252353-explain-me-rotes?p=1252548#post1252548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the answers, I am tempted to use Awakening rules with Ascensions spheres and setting, so I needed some clarifications. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I've been doing with great success. It's a rather easy port, all told.<br /> <br /> I ended up<br /> A) Ditching Wisdom entirely<br /> B) Replacing 'Path' with 'Choose any two ruling Arcana and one inferior'<br /> C) Throwing out the list of Yantras from the book, and replacing them with a mage's choice of 7 Tools from the M20 book, then requiring every spell to include at least one appropriate yantra.<br /> <br /> Let me know how your attempt goes, if you do decide to run it! Always curious to hear about other people using Ascension's setting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}